1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,377
Hi, we are Desert Eagles, and this is Worksight:

2
00:00:03,377 --> 00:00:10,200
visual inspection for quality engineers, built on AMD for the AMD Developer Hackathon, Act Three.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,100
Every new part on a production line needs inspection from day one.

4
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:20,318
But a typical defect model needs many labelled photos of defects and a training run.

5
00:00:20,318 --> 00:00:23,052
Defects are rare, so that data arrives last.

6
00:00:23,052 --> 00:00:26,220
Worksight starts from photos of good parts instead.

7
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:28,091
This is Worksight.

8
00:00:28,091 --> 00:00:30,648
A first-time visitor gets a short tutorial:

9
00:00:30,648 --> 00:00:35,584
what Worksight does, a ready example to try, and how to test with their own photos.

10
00:00:35,584 --> 00:00:39,391
The whole interface speaks six languages, from Italian to Hindi.

11
00:00:39,391 --> 00:00:46,290
And if anything is unclear, the question mark button starts a guided tour that points at each control, step by step.

12
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:52,193
Our demo profile learned from twenty good circuit boards from the public VisA dataset.

13
00:00:52,193 --> 00:00:56,643
It took about nine seconds to build, with no defect labels and no training.

14
00:00:56,643 --> 00:00:59,136
One click inspects a board with bent pins.

15
00:00:59,136 --> 00:01:01,450
In about a second, Worksight says Fail:

16
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:06,256
the anomaly score is above the threshold, and the heatmap sits right on the pins.

17
00:01:06,256 --> 00:01:10,766
Compare puts it next to the closest good board, where the pins are straight.

18
00:01:10,766 --> 00:01:15,750
Original shows the photo alone, and the engineer can zoom in to examine the surface.

19
00:01:16,550 --> 00:01:17,629
Now the AMD part.

20
00:01:17,629 --> 00:01:26,708
Gemma, running on AMD GPUs through AMD Token Factory, sees the photo, the heatmap, the closest good reference and the part's own documentation.

21
00:01:26,708 --> 00:01:28,549
It explains what looks wrong:

22
00:01:28,549 --> 00:01:30,707
the header pins are bent outwards.

23
00:01:30,707 --> 00:01:33,247
And it tells the engineer what to check.

24
00:01:33,247 --> 00:01:36,040
Gemma never changes the detector's decision.

25
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:38,621
The engineer stays in charge.

26
00:01:38,621 --> 00:01:45,497
They choose Pass, Fail or Needs review and add a note, and their decision is stored separately from the model's.

27
00:01:45,497 --> 00:01:54,215
Confirmed good parts can build a new profile version, but it goes live only after it passes a check on a frozen validation set, with rollback.

28
00:01:54,215 --> 00:01:56,180
A good board comes back as Pass.

29
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,025
History keeps every inspection.

30
00:01:59,025 --> 00:02:03,576
Batch inspection checks a whole folder and ranks it by anomaly score.

31
00:02:03,576 --> 00:02:08,456
Part documents, like a specification, give Gemma the context of each part.

32
00:02:08,456 --> 00:02:12,150
And every report can be downloaded as PDF, Word or text.

33
00:02:12,950 --> 00:02:22,668
We measured it on four real circuit board sets from VisA, with a held-out test and every setting chosen on other categories.

34
00:02:22,668 --> 00:02:25,097
AUROC is between 0.88 and 0.99.

35
00:02:25,097 --> 00:02:33,247
Above the threshold alone, Worksight catches 44 to 87 percent of defects at 2 to 6 percent false alarms.

36
00:02:33,247 --> 00:02:38,968
Counting the review band, 56 to 96 percent of defects reach the engineer.

37
00:02:38,968 --> 00:02:42,730
Each inspection takes 0.1 to 0.3 seconds on CPU.

38
00:02:43,530 --> 00:02:48,055
Today, every AI explanation in the live app runs on AMD GPUs.

39
00:02:48,055 --> 00:02:52,358
Next, the detector itself moves to AMD Instinct with ROCm.

40
00:02:52,358 --> 00:02:56,660
The benchmark script is ready, but we have not run it yet.

41
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:04,085
Technavio forecasts the AI visual inspection market to grow by about twenty-seven billion dollars by 2029.

42
00:03:04,085 --> 00:03:09,898
Most tools start from labelled defects, or are code libraries for machine learning engineers.

43
00:03:09,898 --> 00:03:14,210
Worksight starts from good photos and gives the operator a workspace.

44
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:15,659
Our plan:

45
00:03:15,659 --> 00:03:20,993
a subscription per camera view, or an on-premises install on AMD hardware.

46
00:03:20,993 --> 00:03:27,552
First, a pilot on one line, where we measure engineer minutes per part and escaped defects.

47
00:03:27,552 --> 00:03:29,066
We are Desert Eagles:

48
00:03:29,066 --> 00:03:33,391
Bakhtiyar, CEO and AI engineer, and Ali, frontend developer.

49
00:03:33,391 --> 00:03:36,779
Worksight is open source under the MIT license.

50
00:03:36,779 --> 00:03:38,869
Try it at the link on screen.

51
00:03:38,869 --> 00:03:39,590
Thank you.
